Title: Nick and Me
Credit: Written by
Author: Author
Source: Adapted from book
Draft date: 7/30/2026

FADE IN:

INT. PETER AND MA'S APARTMENT - DAY

A modest fifth-floor apartment. PETER (20s), lean but strong, hauls two heavy grocery bags. He struggles with the door.

NICK (20s), broad-shouldered, with a face like a puzzle held together with glue, enters behind him, carrying six bags with ease.

PETER
(V.O.)
Big brother was mine. Nick was the guy everybody was scared of. He had a pair on him the size of steel wrecking balls.

Nick sets the bags down, barely winded. Peter watches him, a mix of admiration and slight fear in his eyes.

PETER
(V.O.)
I lived with him and Ma after dad took off when I was about eight.

INT. MOXIE'S GYM - DAY

A GRUNTING MAN does preacher curls with a 40-pound bar. He sees NICK approach, drops the bar, and offers the bench.

Nick nods, then loads a 50-pound bar for his warm-up. PETER, standing nearby, shakes his head.

PETER
(V.O.)
I’m not too shabby when it comes to weight lifting, but I ain't gonna curl no fifty pounds as a warm-up. Hell, I ain't gonna curl a 50-pound weight probably ever. That’s okay though, Nick is my brother. I know he’ll stand up for me no matter what.

EXT. ALLEY - DAY (FLASHBACK)

YOUNG PETER (8) and YOUNG MARK (8) play kickball. YOUNG NICK (12) watches. Mark kicks the ball hard.

It flies through an open kitchen window in a nearby building. A SHOCKED WOMAN (MRS. ENGEL) appears, furious.

YOUNG MARK
(Terrified)
Oh man!

Young Nick steps forward, facing Mrs. Engel.

YOUNG NICK
I was the one who did it.

Mrs. Engel glares.

PETER
(V.O.)
She called my Ma, and Ma had to pay for the window. Somehow Nick gave her cash to pay for it about a week later. I have no idea where a 12-year old came up with sixty bucks, but I was sure proud of him for that. He never told Ma that it was really Mark who did it. None of us did.

INT. PETER AND MA'S APARTMENT - DAY

MA (60s), frail, with tired brown eyes, shuffles around the kitchen, muttering to herself. Peter watches her.

MA
I can’t find my pain pills, I know I put them here somewhere. Did we go to church today? Did you see Mrs. Canasta there?

Peter points to a pill organizer on the counter, clearly labeled.

PETER
Ma, what are you talking about? We don’t go to church anymore. Your pills are right in front of you in the box for today.

Ma stares at him, her eyes glassy and empty, as if she doesn't recognize him. Then she blinks, snapping out of it.

MA
Oh, right, I am so sorry. I see them right here. I don’t know what got into me.

Peter sighs, worried.

INT. JOE'S BAR AND GRILL - NIGHT

Peter sits at the bar, watching a football game. Nick enters, slaps Peter on the back.

NICK
Hey, little brother. What’s shakin’?

PETER
I don’t know. Nothin’.

NICK
What’s the matter? I can tell you’re hidin’ something. What’s goin’ on?

Peter tells him about Ma's confusion. Nick's face hardens.

NICK
I knew she would start going crazy cooped up in that place all day. Why don’t you take her to the store or something? Holy Christ, do something with her before she turns into some demented old fart and we have to pay for a nursing home or something.

PETER
Of course not. I just needed to get away from her for a while, that’s all.

Nick gives him a look that makes Peter flinch.

NICK
That’s more like it.

Peter pays for his beer, stands.

PETER
(V.O.)
God, sometimes I really hate Nick inside. I mean, he’s done so much for us, but at the same time, inside I really get tired of his shit.

INT. PUBLIC LIBRARY - NIGHT

Peter walks through the grand, old library. High ceilings, old lights on chains, rows of books. He approaches the desk.

PETER
How do I take a book home from here?

LIBRARIAN
Do you have a library card?

PETER
No, how do I get one of those?

The Librarian gives him a form. Peter fills it out, gets a temporary card. He wanders into the "classic literature" section. He picks up "Wuthering Heights."

PETER
(V.O.)
It was about a guy named Heathcliff and a girl named Catherine. So far, it was a little like a soap opera. I got the feeling that these two really loved each other. This reminded me of Sionna.

INT. PETER'S BEDROOM - NIGHT

Peter lies in bed, "Wuthering Heights" open on his chest. He closes his eyes.

He's on horseback, riding through a lush, ancient forest. SIONNA (20s), in old-fashioned clothes, sits in front of him. He holds her waist, leaning in to smell her neck.

They emerge into a sun-drenched field. Peter helps Sionna down. He looks into her light blue eyes. They embrace and kiss.

PETER
(V.O.)
I am falling in love with this woman. Never have I been this vulnerable, allowing a woman to take all of my strength.

Peter bolts upright in bed, sweating, heart pounding.

PETER
(V.O.)
What the hell was that? It was Sionna, but in a different place with old clothes on. What is happening?

INT. THE JAVA HUT - DAY

Peter sits opposite SIONNA at a small table. She sips coffee.

PETER
(V.O.)
When I looked into her eyes, I lost all track of time and forgot who I was and what I was doing. I decided, she really was beautiful.

SIONNA
What are you reading right now?

PETER
Wuthering Heights. It’s the story of this guy and girl and how they grew apart but were really in love with each other.

SIONNA
Yea, I know. I read it.

Peter blushes. Sionna talks about the book's themes.

SIONNA
The environment of the book was like its people. They were wild and unpredictable and infertile. The love that Heathcliff has for Catherine never changes, but in the end that kind of love destroys him. A love that never changes will destroy you.

Peter considers this, looking at her intently.

PETER
(V.O.)
It reminded me of the way Nick is; strong and unwavering, but somehow it seemed dumb. I wondered if it would destroy him in the end too.

INT. DOCTOR'S OFFICE - DAY

Peter sits opposite DR. CARSON (50s), a kind but serious man.

DR. CARSON
Your mother’s blood pressure is dangerously high. It’s so high, I’m afraid of the risk of a stroke. My advice is that you take her directly to the emergency room and we admit her for observation.

Peter is stunned.

PETER
Whoa man. I can’t believe this. Are you sure it’s that bad?

DR. CARSON
Your mother has been confused, is that right? And she also experienced chest pressure this afternoon?

PETER
Yeah, that’s right. She hasn’t been acting too normal lately.

Peter calls Nick, who is clearly annoyed.

PETER
(V.O.)
I hated to tell him the hundreds of times she didn’t act normal. I forgot what it was like for her to act normal anyway.

INT. HOSPITAL ROOM - NIGHT

Ma sleeps in a hospital bed. Peter dozes in a chair.

He dreams he is a SOLDIER in a chaotic battlefield. Blood and screaming. He stands over a dying man.

DYING MAN
Save her...

The man dies. Peter turns. NICK, in soldier's gear, runs towards him.

PETER
Nick! Nick! Thank God you’re here! I thought I was going to die.

NICK
(Hissing)
That you are little brother.

Nick plunges a long knife into Peter's chest. Peter gasps.

Peter wakes up, gasping for breath, heart pounding. He's still in the hospital room. Ma is still sleeping.

PETER
(V.O.)
Why would Nick want to kill me? Me? His little brother. I felt betrayed and so confused.

INT. PETER AND MA'S APARTMENT - NIGHT

Ma sits in her chair, looking at a new pill organizer. SIONNA stands beside her, explaining it.

SIONNA
See Ma, right here is every day of the week, and every day will have the pills in you need. There’s even separations for morning and night.

MA
Oh my Lord, that looks a little overwhelming.

PETER
No worries Ma. I’m goin’ to be here to make sure everything is okay.

Ma looks at Peter, then Sionna.

MA
You’re such a good boy. You and Nick are like a God-send to me. What would I do without you two?

Peter looks at Sionna, a flicker of resentment for Ma's comment. The door slams open. NICK enters, face beet red, hair wild.

NICK
What’s up little Bro? You got Ma all tucked in? Man, you shoulda been a nurse!

PETER
(Accusingly)
Knock it off man. Somebody has to make sure she stays on track. Where have you been?

NICK
Don’t start giving ME shit Bro. Where the hell do you think? I was at work. More than you can say for your sorry ass down at that bullshit pizza parlor job.

Nick's face gets redder. He kicks his boots onto a footstool.

NICK
(CONT'D)
Are you going to keep her from strokin’ out, or what?

Peter hands him the pill organizer.

PETER
Look – I got her meds all in the same spot, and told her I would help her keep track of everything. Check it out.

NICK
Oh, holy shit! Aren’t you nurse Nancy! Well, well, how did you come up with this little idea anyway?

PETER
(Through gritted teeth)
If you must know, Sionna helped me figure it out. She’s really smart and good at that shit.

NICK
(Mockingly)
This chick sure has you wrapped around her finger. I mean, if you must know.

PETER
(Voice rising)
Stop it Nick! You haven’t even met her. I don’t understand how you can’t like someone you don’t even know, Man. Give her a fuckin’ break!

NICK
(Standing, towering over Peter)
Don’t you talk to me like that, you little bastard.

PETER
I’m not a bastard!

NICK
How the hell do you know? Maybe you are. You sure are a giant pussy – and that makes you and me way different Bro.

PETER
(Screaming)
You’re so Goddamn hateful. What the fuck got into you? Was Ma on crack or somethin’ when she was pregnant with you?

WHACK! Nick's hand slaps Peter across the head. Peter's ear rings. Nick spins and stomps out, slamming the door.

PETER
(V.O.)
Christ, what just happened? I had never been in a screaming fight with Nick before. It just came bubbling out of me like I had been holding it down forever.

INT. PETER AND MA'S APARTMENT - DAY

SIONNA sits with MA, who is laughing gently.

MA
On Halloween, we would watch from the bushes, and my brothers would tip those outhouses over!

Peter smiles, watching Ma animatedly tell stories of her childhood. Nick enters. Ma is overjoyed.

MA
Oh My God! It’s you Nick! I thought we would never see you again.

Sionna walks in with two plates of peach pie. She offers her hand to Nick.

SIONNA
I’m Sionna. You must be Nick. Nice to meet you, I’ve heard so much about you.

NICK
(Reluctantly shaking her hand)
Uh, yea, likewise.

SIONNA
You’re just in time for pie.

NICK
No thanks. I can’t eat that crap. Sugar makes me feel bloated and sick.

Nick stares Sionna up and down.

NICK
So, I hear you’re a university lady.

SIONNA
That’s right.

NICK
What are you gonna do when you get done? It’s tough out there, and, like I was tellin’ my kid brother here….sometimes all that school just doesn’t pay off. It’s even harder for a woman to teach at that level, or so I’ve heard.

Sionna sets her plate down, a polite smile on her face.

SIONNA
Well, Nick, I have to disagree with you there. As a matter of fact, in the last forty years, bachelor’s degrees earned by female students have risen from about 35 to 55 percent. You can’t keep a good woman down, so to speak.

Nick is visibly stunned. Sionna picks up Ma's plate and heads to the kitchen.

NICK
(To Peter, voice low)
Well, if you ask me, that might be one of the reasons this country is heading down the flippin’ tubes. The women in this country can’t stay home and take care of their kids.

Sionna returns.

SIONNA
But I would have to disagree with you that this is purely the reason for a failing society. Women in the area of education are adding other dimensions to the learning environment that have enriched the lives of students. Diversity helps us learn.

She walks back into the kitchen. Peter is beaming.

PETER
(V.O.)
Inside I was jumping up and down, and yelling “that’s my girl!” I was so proud of her at that moment. Nick was sitting there stunned.

Nick stands, gives Ma a peck on the cheek.

NICK
Well, I guess I better get going. Someone in this room has a job they have to go to tomorrow. Sounds like you two have it all figured out, with help of course from Doctor Sionna.

His sarcasm hangs in the air. Sionna re-enters.

SIONNA
Oh gosh, are you leaving already? We hardly had a chance to talk at all.

NICK
Um, yeah. Well, I’m sure I’ll see you around. Take care of this numbskull.

Nick grabs Peter's shoulders, jiggles him. Peter's eyes meet Sionna's, her face a calm pool of water. Nick whispers to Peter.

NICK
(CONT'D)
Take care of Ma.

PETER
Nick, you know I will.

Peter watches Nick walk down the hallway, already pulling out a cigarette.

PETER
(V.O.)
More and more, his presence made me sick. It was this feeling in the pit of my stomach like there was too much bile. Like I didn’t need him anymore.

INT. PETER AND MA'S APARTMENT - DAY

Peter enters the silent apartment. He calls out for Ma. No answer. He searches. Her purse, coat, nothing.

He sees the blinking red light on the answering machine. He presses play.

OFFICER DUPUIS (V.O.)
Mr. Olson, this is Officer Mike Dupuis from the Milwaukee County Sheriff's Department. We need to talk to you regarding your family.

NURSE OWENS (V.O.)
Hello Mr. Olson, this is Patricia Owens, one of the nurses at Frodo Hospital, with an update on your family members.

Peter's face drains of color. He rewinds, copies the number. He calls.

INT. POLICE STATION - DAY

Peter sits opposite OFFICER DUPUIS (50s), a grave expression on his face.

OFFICER DUPUIS
Mr. Olson, it seems that there has been a serious accident involving your brother, Mr. Nicholas Olson, and your mother, a Mrs. Olivia Olson. Last night about 8 p.m. they were hit broadside while going through the intersection of Werner and Lowe.

Peter holds his breath.

OFFICER DUPUIS (CONT'D)
I regret to tell you that your brother is in serious condition at Frodo and your mother passed away at the scene. Her body is at Sacred Heart Funeral Home.

Peter feels a wave of nausea. He asks for water.

PETER
(V.O.)
He continued to talk, but I have no recollection of what he said. Everything is a blur.

He calls Sionna, leaves a frantic message.

INT. PETER AND MA'S APARTMENT - NIGHT

Peter sits in Ma's empty chair, staring at it. He starts to cry, a raw, guttural sound.

PETER
(Screaming into the empty room)
She was dead. And Nick killed her. He fucking killed my mom. Die you fucking jackass. Die. Die.

SIONNA enters, finds Peter sobbing. She holds him, stroking his head.

SIONNA
Just let it out. Let it out. We'll figure it all out. Don't worry.

EXT. CATHOLIC CEMETERY - DAY

A small group gathers for Ma's graveside service. Peter, Sionna, and BOB are present. Peter reluctantly throws a handful of dirt onto the light maple-colored casket. It hits with a muted thunk.

BOB
(To Peter, solemn)
I’m checking on Nick all the time and would watch over his apartment.

Peter nods, numb.

PETER
(V.O.)
I was really behind on schoolwork and sleep. I probably had about 4 hours a night since this all went down.

INT. HOSPITAL ROOM - DAY

Peter enters Nick's hospital room. Nick is propped up, sallow, bruised, with tubes. His right leg is huge under the bedspread.

NICK
(Weak voice)
Hey, bro. I guess I really fucked up, man. Can't believe it. Can't believe Ma's gone.

Tears stream down Nick's face. Peter is silent.

PETER
They took care of it. The mass was nice. She's at peace now. The plot is at the top of the hill at St. Mary's, flat stone near some trees. She's okay.

NICK
I didn't mean to have 3 Jack and Cokes before he remembered he needed to take her to church. The cops are after me now. They're telling me it could be vehicular manslaughter.

PETER
(Dead-on stare)
Whose fault was it, Nick?

NICK
(Furious)
What do you mean? You think I meant to kill her? You think I meant to kill Ma? You son of a bitch.

Peter realizes Nick's rage is powerless now.

PETER
Think about it, Nick.

Peter turns and leaves.

PETER
(V.O.)
I no longer gave two shits about Nick. All of his upcoming legal battles can be fought alone for all I care. I lost my mom, and it seemed I had also lost my brother.

INT. SIONNA'S APARTMENT - DAY

NICK (POV) enters Sionna's apartment. He sees dead plants on the porch. He knocks. SIONNA opens the door a crack.

SIONNA
Nick? Is that you? Oh my gosh. I never would have expected you here.

She opens the door. Nick steps inside. A gray cat sulks away.

NICK
(Angry)
I don't suppose you have any idea what the fuck I've been going through lately, do you? You're the reason I'm probably going to jail. You know that?

SIONNA
(Calmly)
Let's talk about this rationally. What makes you think I'm responsible for you going to jail?

Nick inches closer, hovering over her.

NICK
If it wasn't for you messing around with my brother, everything would be cool. He would be taking care of ma. She would be alive right now and I would be working.

He spits a little. Sionna wipes her face, tries to move past him. Nick blocks her, pushing her against the wall.

NICK
(CONT'D)
How about paying for my hospital and lawyer bills? You got 20 grand? This is all your fault. You got two things to do right now. You come up with some money, and you get the fuck away from my brother. Stay out of his life.

SIONNA
Nick, calm down. This really has nothing to do with me.

Nick grabs her neck with his left hand. She makes squeaking noises. He pulls a switchblade from his pocket, flicks it open in front of her face. Her eyes widen.

NICK
(CONT'D)
Now you're listening, aren't you? This is so you can remember how serious I am. Break it off with him tonight or else. Then you're going to get your hands on some cash and get ready to hand it over. I'll be back in one week and I better see some fucking cash or this blade goes into your little neck.

Sionna nods, face white.

SUDDENLY, the front door THUNKS open. PETER stands there, horrified.

PETER
Holy shit, Nick, what the fuck are you doing?

Peter lunges for Nick's arm. Nick struggles, elbowing Peter in the head. The knife hits Sionna hard. Red sprays out. She makes a weird noise, sinking to the floor.

Nick wipes the blade on her shirt, then runs out. Peter rushes to Sionna, frantically ripping her shirt to find the wound. He presses both hands on her left shoulder. Sirens wail in the distance.

PETER
(V.O.)
My brother stabbed her. He stabbed her. Oh God, will she die?

INT. HOSPITAL ROOM - DAY

Sionna lies in a hospital bed, her shoulder bandaged. Peter sits beside her. She looks at him, her eyes blank.

SIONNA
I can't feel me. I can't feel myself anymore.

PETER
(Squatting to face her)
Please know that I love you. You are safe. I will protect you with my life.

SIONNA
You say that, but deep inside I still have my doubts. As long as there is any doubt, I can't go on with you. Maybe we just need a break so I can hash things out with a therapist. Go to Mom and Dad's for a while.

Peter's eyes well up.

PETER
Sionna, don't do that. Stay here with me and we can work things out. Please?

Sionna slowly walks into the bedroom. Peter hangs his head, tearing at his hair.

PETER
(V.O.)
My fingers were slipping slowly and painfully off the rocky cliff. I had no one now. My exit from the house was a free fall into the black, endless void of space.

EXT. SEATTLE STREETS - DAY (7 YEARS LATER)

Seven years later. PETER (30s), now well-dressed, walks through bustling Seattle streets. He owns a chain of pizzerias. He passes a woman with dark brown hair, instantly reminded of SIONNA.

PETER
(V.O.)
Seven years of change, seven years of loneliness, and seven years of hatred for my brother.

INT. PETER'S SEATTLE APARTMENT - NIGHT

Peter sits on his couch. His cat, BOZO, is curled up. Peter closes his eyes.

He is in a magical place, winding dirt roads, rolling green hills. A SAGE, with dark skin and a white flowing wrap, walks beside him.

SAGE
Stop judging things. This is not your place. It is below you. Set your inner sight higher, and no things are neither good nor bad. This is an illusion.

Peter bows his head. When he looks up, the Sage is gone. Peter feels alive, optimistic, joyful.

PETER
(V.O.)
I had to change. I had to start living again. I had to find forgiveness.

INT. CORRECTIONAL INSTITUTE - VISITING ROOM - DAY

Peter sits in a stark visiting room, a thick plexiglass barrier between him and NICK. Nick looks older, gaunt, graying hair, sad eyes.

NICK
(Gravelly voice)
Hi, bro. Glad you came.

PETER
Hi, Nick. Good to see you finally. How are you holding up?

NICK
It's not a cakewalk, but I got my routine down. It's looking pretty good for getting out early. Maybe as early as 2 more years.

PETER
(V.O.)
I weighed this in my mind. What did I care? I probably would never see him again anyway.

PETER
(CONT'D)
Well, that's good for you, Nick. Good for you. I'm here to tell you some things. And I would appreciate it if you would just listen to me.

Nick nods, resigned.

PETER
(CONT'D)
I am no longer interested in seeing you or hearing anything you have to say to me. You're an asshole that killed my mother in a drunk driving accident. You're an asshole that held me down my entire life. But mostly, you're an asshole for trying to kill the love of my life, which drove her away. I'll never see you again because of you, Nick. Because you're an asshole.

Peter takes a deep breath.

PETER
(CONT'D)
Now that you know how I feel about you, I have to add this bit, and this is the most important bit, so I want you to remember this. I forgive you. I forgive you for being a huge asshole because it sets me free. It sets me free to never have anger or regret or feelings of loss. I forgive you, Nick, because it also releases your control over me forever, and that's what I need.

Nick stares at the counter, then looks up, tears streaming down his face.

NICK
I'm so sorry. You're so right, man. I did do all that shit. I am a huge asshole. I feel so bad about Ma and Sionna. You're more than I ever was, you know. You're a big man, and I'm a small one.

A GUARD approaches.

GUARD
Time's almost up.

PETER
(To Nick)
After all is said and done, I want you to get better. I still believe in you. I still love you for being my brother. Do you hear me?

NICK
I hear you, man. I love you too. Say, what are you doing now?

PETER
I own a pizza chain in Seattle and we'll be expanding. You always said I couldn't do it. I did it, Nick. I really did it.

NICK
Wow, man. President Olson. That's fucking amazing. I am so proud of you, man. I love you.

The guard signals time is up. Nick smiles, a genuine, sad smile.

NICK
Bye.

Peter smiles back, hangs up the phone, watches Nick being led away.

PETER
(V.O.)
I had finished my quest and felt completely exonerated. That part of my life was closed now, and it was a complete relief.

EXT. WISCONSIN COUNTRYSIDE - DAY

Peter drives through rolling hills, the weight of years lifted. He feels light, free.

PETER
(V.O.)
Somewhere, she's out there. She's happy. I just know it. I have to believe that. I hope she believes that I'm happy too. The weight of 30 years was gone, and I was free to live without fear, guilt, sadness, or judgment.

He looks at his boarding pass.

PETER
(V.O.)
President Olson. That's me. President Peter Olson. This has been Nick and me.

FADE OUT.
